Subject: [PATCH] Fix two claims in ch 0.2 flagged by fact-check

- 'NDB' is not a Nepali hydropower lender (Nepal is not a BRICS NDB
  member); the institutional co-lenders are HIDCL and Nepal
  Infrastructure Bank (NIFRA), alongside ADB/World Bank/bilaterals
- The MFI squeeze passage still described a fixed lending-rate cap with
  zero pass-through; since Shrawan 2082 (July 2025) that flat 15% cap was
  replaced by a base-rate-plus-premium regime (which chapters 31/73/85
  already describe correctly) - reworded so ch 0.2 no longer contradicts
  them, while keeping the (true) point that the squeeze persists
---
 investors-canon/book.html                             | 6 +++---
 investors-canon/chapters/ch-0-2-nrb-transmission.html | 6 +++---
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

